" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f51647-bae7-5532-b804-b3b54fdccc4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141200/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-141200/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-141200/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-141200/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141200/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-141200/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141200" :question/id #uuid "95fb61ee-6372-5926-b11d-d18f6bad7442" :question/math-academy-id "q-141200" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $\\text{Null}(A)={0}$\n- $\\text{nullity}(A)=6$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "fb2ca3e6-3016-52bb-93ac-cf5addf3c8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f4bbb2b9-d256-5c64-bd14-99273892263f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f76a542b-1405-5ac5-bbf2-dcf467246fec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "461740ba-304c-580c-b0bc-3441fd162292" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "000fec77-bea3-5b1e-b69c-342c6527bcc5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6b2619-8d04-5edb-8689-da6db3e8af02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142358/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-142358/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-142358/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-142358/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-142358/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-142358/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142358" :question/id #uuid "9de3bb13-65d5-5b1c-b866-679fe9bf3723" :question/math-academy-id "q-142358" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n\n- $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- $A$ is  invertible\n- $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142358/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142358"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "947919d2-63e1-5774-b9bd-af379aeb50e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e2ef2978-6469-5b50-bb76-9cfa29f42b1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "cb69d318-2175-5a82-a86a-deca237f31d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "75e32c15-af80-5d43-b41a-6e3c9b3a99c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "123fc04e-4909-5609-aee0-32b5f60b795e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7082c85f-a381-57a4-a45b-30ec8ba228b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141199/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-141199/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141199/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-141199/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-141199/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141199/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141199" :question/id #uuid "7c701e87-53a1-5406-ab33-1b75f3ea593b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141199" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\n- $\\text{Null}(A)={0}$\n- $A$ is not invertible\n- $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne {0},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141199/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f4276993-4c56-519f-b025-2850b8913d9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "1a9d9a60-34d8-5050-bf02-51f9eb9c1493" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3db264c1-f171-57eb-b0ed-3dd6b9081b80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "fa9a564f-ae9a-57e3-8171-563ca3cdf256" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "aabbc51c-60f1-5bed-b20c-fec002483c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bfa085-a8c7-507c-af46-3f860c19c809" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142474/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-142474/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-142474/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-142474/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-142474/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-142474/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142474" :question/id #uuid "7804590c-275e-53bf-9345-63a0af840940" :question/math-academy-id "q-142474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n\n- $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142474/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35425/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8e140777-add1-5998-b9fa-b0414f93a4c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35425/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1d1700d2-29ed-53bf-8abc-bfc124bf80cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35425/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "b4e119a2-0cac-55bc-ac7a-387d109f79c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35425/selection/df67a18079e3b7b72